      "summary_markdown": "- SLA breach concentration is strongly associated with high ticket reassignments (reassignment count = 3+ shows a 28.8% missed SLA rate versus 9.7% for count = 1).\n- Missed SLA rates vary by category, ranging from 12.0% in hardware to 19.3% in network, with the Network Operations assignment group reaching 22.1%.\n- Priority-1 records concentrate in specific segments: the top 3 CMDB CI name segments account for 46.7% of 694 priority-1 records (Gini 0.57).\n- Payments Gateway priority-1 incidents show severe assignment group concentration, with the top 3 groups accounting for 83.4% of 271 incidents (Gini 0.66).\n- Recommended next steps: Review configuration management for high-volume CMDB CI segments, investigate workflows in the network category and Network Operations group, and optimize routing to reduce excessive reassignments.",
      "verified_insights": 5
    },
